@*
    UK 14-day cancellation-right notice (spec §2.4 & §4). Shown pre-payment (cart + order-confirm)
    so the statutory cancellation right is visible before the customer pays. Content/link only —
    no checkout flow, step, or field change.

    The link points at the store's Conditions of Use topic (the only guaranteed-present policy topic
    in nopCommerce's default data, and already used by the checkout terms link). A merchant who adds a
    dedicated Returns / Cancellation Policy topic can repoint this single partial at it.
*@
<div class="ft-cancellation-notice" role="note">
    <span class="ft-cancellation-notice__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v5" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="0.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>
    </span>
    <span class="ft-cancellation-notice__text">
        <strong>14-day cancellation right.</strong>
        You can cancel your order within 14 days of delivery under UK consumer law.
        <a href="@await NopUrl.RouteTopicUrlAsync("conditionsofuse")" class="ft-cancellation-notice__link">See our cancellation &amp; returns policy</a>.
    </span>
</div>
